                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "How Anchoring Works",
                                    content: "When making numerical estimates, we start from an initial value (the anchor) and adjust from there. The problem? **We adjust insufficiently.**\n\nKahneman and Tversky's experiment:\n• Group A: 'Is the % of African nations in UN more or less than 10%? What's your estimate?'\n• Group B: 'Is it more or less than 65%? What's your estimate?'\n\nGroup A's average estimate: 25%\nGroup B's average estimate: 45%\n\nA completely arbitrary anchor shifted estimates by 20 percentage points."
