                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Two Types of Anchoring",
                                    content: "**1. Anchoring as Adjustment** (System 2)\nYou start at the anchor and deliberately adjust. But adjustment is effortful, so you stop too soon. Like pulling a rubber band - the anchor pulls you back.\n\n**2. Anchoring as Priming** (System 1)\nThe anchor activates compatible information. Ask 'Is Gandhi older than 144 when he died?' and your mind retrieves thoughts of old Gandhi, ancient wisdom, longevity - biasing subsequent estimates upward."
