                                    title: "How Availability Works",
                                    content: "We estimate the frequency of events based on how easily examples come to mind. Easy to recall = must be common.\n\n**Why does this fail?**\n\nThings are easy to recall when they're:\n• Recent (you just heard about it)\n• Emotional (scary, dramatic, vivid)\n• Personal (happened to you or someone you know)\n• Repeated (media coverage)\n\nNone of these correlate with actual frequency. Media coverage ≠probability."
