                                    content: "Imagine a vacation where you have an amazing time, but at the end you'll be given a drug that erases all memory of it. Would you still go? Most people say no - revealing that we don't optimize for experience, but for memory. You have an experiencing self that lives your life, and a remembering self that writes the story. They want different things.",
