                                    content: "Of all GTD's insights, the Two-Minute Rule is the most widely adopted. The concept is elegantly simple: if an action will take less than two minutes to complete, do it immediately. Don't add it to a list. Don't defer it. Just do it. This single habit can transform your productivity and eliminate the small-task backlog that creates overwhelm."
