                                    title: "EMDR: Processing Without Words",
                                    content: "**Eye Movement Desensitization and Reprocessing**\n\n**How it works:**\n• Hold traumatic memory in mind\n• Follow therapist's finger (bilateral stimulation)\n• Brain processes the memory differently\n• Distress reduces rapidly\n\n**Why it works:**\n• May simulate REM sleep processing\n• Keeps 'watchtower' (prefrontal cortex) online\n• Allows memory to be filed as 'past'\n\n**Results:**\n• Often works faster than talk therapy\n• Especially effective for single-incident trauma\n• Strong research support"
