                                    title: "Internal Family Systems (IFS)",
                                    content: "**IFS views the mind as containing multiple 'parts':**\n\n**Exiles:** Parts holding pain and trauma\n**Managers:** Parts trying to control and protect\n**Firefighters:** Parts that numb or distract\n**Self:** The core, wise, compassionate center\n\n**Healing process:**\n1. Access the Self (calm, curious, compassionate)\n2. Build relationship with protective parts\n3. Safely approach wounded/exiled parts\n4. Allow healing and integration\n\n**Why it works for trauma:** Honors ALL parts as trying to help, reduces internal warfare."
