                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Not Too Much (The Lost Art of Eating)",
                                    content: "**Americans have forgotten how to eat:**\n• We eat too fast\n• We eat too much\n• We eat everywhere (cars, desks, standing)\n• We eat alone\n\n**The Okinawan principle: Hara hachi bu**\n'Eat until you're 80% full'\n\n**Why this works:**\n• Takes 20 minutes for satiety signals to reach brain\n• Stopping at 80% prevents overeating\n• Okinawans have world's highest life expectancy\n\n**The mindful approach:** Slow down, pay attention, enjoy."
