                                    title: "The Bohr Effect: Why CO2 Matters",
                                    content: "**The Bohr Effect** explains why CO2 is essential:\n\nOxygen binds tightly to hemoglobin. For oxygen to be RELEASED to your tissues, you need adequate CO2.\n\n**Low CO2 means:**\n• Oxygen stays bound to hemoglobin\n• Tissues don't get enough oxygen\n• You feel breathless (even though blood is saturated)\n• You breathe more (making it worse)\n\n**Optimal CO2 means:**\n• Oxygen releases easily to tissues\n• You feel calm and clear\n• You need fewer breaths\n• Better endurance and energy"
