                                    content: "**The quality paradox:**\n\nMVPs seem low quality, but they test **the right things**.\n\nBuilding a \"complete\" product before testing is:\n- More expensive to build\n- More expensive to change\n- More painful to throw away\n\n**Quality isn't about features—it's about learning.**\n\nAn MVP that teaches you something valuable is higher quality than a polished product nobody wants."
