                                    type: "example",
                                    title: "The Fish Analogy",
                                    content: "**Carnegie's fishing wisdom:**\n\n*\"When I go fishing, I don't bait the hook with strawberries and cream—even though that's what I like. I bait it with what the fish wants: worms.\"*\n\n**The lesson:**\nStop thinking about what you want. Start thinking about what the other person wants.\n\n**In practice:**\n- Before asking for something, ask yourself: \"What does this person want?\"\n- Frame requests in terms of their benefits\n- Help them see how helping you helps them"
