                                    content: "In the 1970s, a bank robbery in Chase Manhattan went wrong. Hostages were taken. The police tried the standard approach: demand surrender, threaten force.\n\n**Result**: Disaster. The situation escalated.\n\nThis led to a revolution in hostage negotiation. The FBI developed new techniques based on:\n- Active listening\n- Building rapport\n- Understanding emotions\n\nThese techniques later proved just as effective in business negotiations, salary discussions, and everyday conflicts."
