                                    title: "Why No Feels Safe",
                                    content: "\"No\" protects people. When someone says no, they feel:\n\n- **In control** of their boundaries\n- **Safe** from commitment\n- **Autonomous** and respected\n\nOnce they feel safe, they're more willing to listen and eventually say a genuine yes.\n\n**Tactical application**: Instead of asking, *\"Do you have a few minutes to talk?\"* ask:\n\n*\"Is now a bad time to talk?\"*\n\nYou invite a \"no,\" which makes them feel in control. Then they're more open to continuing."
