                                    content: "There are two words that, when your counterpart says them, signal a breakthrough:\n\n**\"That's right.\"**\n\nNot \"you're right\" (that's dismissive). Not \"yes\" (that might be fake). But **\"that's right\"**—the signal that they feel truly understood.\n\nWhen someone says \"that's right,\" they've just confirmed that you've accurately summarized their world. Trust skyrockets. Walls come down."
