                                    title: "Bending Reality at the Car Dealer",
                                    content: "**Traditional approach**: *\"I'd like to pay $25,000 for this car.\"*\nDealer: *\"Lowest we can go is $28,000.\"*\nYou split the difference: $26,500.\n\n**Bending reality approach**:\n\n1. **Anchor extreme**: *\"Based on comparable vehicles and known issues with this model year, I'm thinking $22,000.\"*\n\n2. **Frame as loss**: *\"Every day this sits on your lot costs you money in financing and depreciation.\"*\n\n3. **Odd number**: *\"I can do $24,350 right now.\"* (Specific numbers seem more researched)\n\nResult: $24,350 vs $26,500 = **$2,150 saved** by bending reality."
