                                    content: "**Reality isn't fixed—it's framed.**\n\nThe same deal can feel terrible or excellent depending on how it's presented. Ethical negotiators use these techniques:\n\n- **Loss framing** - Show what they lose by not acting\n- **Extreme anchoring** - Set the range in your favor\n- **Specific numbers** - Signal research and legitimacy\n- **Real deadlines** - Create appropriate urgency\n\n*\"Never split the difference\"* isn't about being stubborn—it's about shaping how the other side sees the deal so splitting isn't necessary."
