                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "The Armor We Wear",
                                    content: "**Common vulnerability shields:**\n\n**Foreboding joy:** Waiting for the other shoe to drop; not letting yourself feel happiness\n\n**Perfectionism:** Armor that says 'if I look perfect, I won't be hurt'\n\n**Numbing:** Using food, work, alcohol to avoid feeling\n\n**Cynicism:** 'Cool' distancing that prevents getting hurt\n\n**Criticism:** Putting others down to elevate yourself\n\n**The cost:**\nThese shields don't protect us—they isolate us from connection, creativity, and real leadership."
