                                    title: "Shitty First Drafts (SFD)",
                                    content: "When something happens, we immediately create a story about it. These first drafts are usually wrong—they're written by our fear, insecurity, and past hurts.\n\n**Example:**\nYou give a presentation and the boss seems distracted.\n\n**SFD (Shitty First Draft):**\n\"They hated it. They think I'm incompetent. I'm going to get fired.\"\n\n**After rumbling with reality:**\n\"They seemed distracted. I don't actually know why. Maybe they had something else on their mind. I could ask for feedback.\"\n\n**The practice:**\nCapture your SFD, then challenge it with curiosity."
