                                    content: "Humans have enormous brains—2-3% of body weight but consuming 25% of our energy. This came at huge costs:\n\n**Trade-off 1: Weak Bodies**\nEnergy went to brains, not muscles. A chimp can easily overpower a human.\n\n**Trade-off 2: Dangerous Childbirth**\nBig brains mean big heads. Humans give birth earlier than other apes (babies are helpless), and childbirth is dangerous.\n\n**Trade-off 3: Long Dependency**\nHuman children need care for YEARS. Most animals walk within hours of birth.\n\n**The irony:** For 2 million years, our big brains didn't make us dominant. We were middle-of-the-food-chain scavengers, cracking bones for marrow after lions finished eating."
