                                    type: "example",
                                    title: "Peugeot: A Legal Fiction",
                                    content: "Consider Peugeot, the car company. Where does it exist?\n\n**Not in its cars** - Destroy all Peugeots, the company survives.\n**Not in its factories** - Sell the factories, the company survives.\n**Not in its employees** - Fire everyone, the company survives.\n**Not in its founders** - They're long dead.\n\nPeugeot exists as a **legal fiction**—a story we all agree to believe. A lawyer performed rituals (incorporation), wrote spells (legal documents), and poof—a new entity was born.\n\n**The insight:** We've been creating 'imagined orders' for 70,000 years. First gods, then nations, now corporations. They're all the same type of thing: powerful fictions."
