                                    content: "**Exercise: Spot the fictions in your life**\n\n1. **Money** - Why does paper have value? Only because we agree it does.\n\n2. **Your job** - Companies are legal fictions. So is your 'career.'\n\n3. **National identity** - Being 'American' or 'French' is a story.\n\n4. **Human rights** - Beautiful fiction, but not found in nature.\n\n**Why this matters:**\nFictions aren't lies—they're tools. Understanding them as tools gives you power:\n• To question which fictions serve you\n• To choose which stories to believe\n• To recognize when fictions harm people\n\n**The goal isn't cynicism—it's clarity.**"
