                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "The Luxury Trap",
                                    content: "**How the trap worked:**\n\n1. Some foragers noticed wheat growing wild. Easy calories!\n\n2. They started tending the wheat. A little more work, but more food.\n\n3. More food â†’ more babies surviving.\n\n4. More babies â†’ need even more food â†’ more farming.\n\n5. Soon, too many people to go back to foraging.\n\n**The trap:** Each 'improvement' created new needs that locked in more work.\n\n**Sound familiar?** This pattern repeats throughout history:\n• Email was supposed to save time â†’ Now we're drowning in messages\n• Cars were supposed to give freedom â†’ Now we're stuck in traffic\n• Smartphones were supposed to simplify life â†’ Now we're addicted\n\n**Harari's insight:** 'Luxuries tend to become necessities and to spawn new obligations.'"
