                                    type: "intro",
                                    title: "In the Beginning...",
                                    content: "13.8 billion years ago, everything we know—every star, planet, atom, and the space between them—was compressed into an unimaginably dense point smaller than a proton. Then, in a moment beyond comprehension, it began to expand. Not an explosion INTO space, but an expansion OF space itself.\n\nThis wasn't just the birth of matter and energy. It was the birth of space and time. Before this moment, there was no 'before'—time itself didn't exist. The universe didn't expand into something; it created the something as it expanded.\n\nEvery atom in your body, the oxygen you breathe, the iron in your blood—all of it traces back to this singular moment. You are quite literally made of the universe. Let's explore how it all began."
