                                    content: "Look at your hand. The calcium in your bones was forged in the heart of a star. The iron in your blood came from a supernova explosion. The oxygen you're breathing right now was created in the nuclear furnace of a stellar core.\n\nStars aren't just pretty lights in the sky—they're cosmic factories that transform simple hydrogen into every element on the periodic table (except hydrogen itself). Without stars, the universe would be nothing but a sea of hydrogen and helium gas. No planets. No life. No you.\n\nStars live, age, and die in spectacular fashion—and in their deaths, they seed the cosmos with the building blocks of everything complex. Let's explore these magnificent engines of creation."
