                                    type: "intro",
                                    title: "The Ultimate Cosmic Extremes",
                                    content: "Imagine a place where gravity is so intense that nothing—not light, not information, not even time as we know it—can escape. A place where the known laws of physics break down. A place that might connect to other universes, or destroy anything that enters, or both.\n\nBlack holes sound like science fiction, but they're very real. They're born from the deaths of massive stars, lurk at the centers of most galaxies, and have been directly imaged for the first time in 2019. They're the universe's most extreme objects—cosmic laboratories where Einstein's theories are pushed to their limits.\n\nBlack holes are simultaneously the darkest objects in the universe and among the most energetic, powering quasars visible across billions of light-years. Let's explore these fascinating cosmic monsters."
