                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "The Milky Way: Our Home Galaxy",
                                    content: "We live in a **barred spiral galaxy** about 100,000-180,000 light-years in diameter:\n\n**Structure:**\n• **Disk**: Thin plane of stars, gas, dust; spiral arms with active star formation\n• **Bulge**: Dense central region, older stars, bar-shaped\n• **Halo**: Sparse spherical region; old stars, globular clusters\n• **Dark matter halo**: Extends far beyond visible matter\n\n**Our Location:**\n• Orion Arm (minor arm between Sagittarius and Perseus arms)\n• About 26,000 light-years from the center\n• Orbital period around galaxy: ~230 million years ('galactic year')\n• The Sun has orbited ~20 times since formation\n\n**Central Black Hole:**\n• Sagittarius A* (Sgr A*)\n• 4 million solar masses\n• Event horizon: ~24 million km\n• Currently quiet, but has flared in the past\n\n**Neighbors:**\n• Magellanic Clouds: Irregular dwarf galaxies, satellites of the Milky Way\n• Andromeda (M31): Nearest large galaxy, 2.5 million light-years away, approaching us"
