                                    content: "Galaxies change dramatically over cosmic time:\n\n**Hierarchical Assembly:**\n• Small galaxies form first from primordial gas\n• They merge to form larger galaxies\n• The Milky Way has absorbed dozens of smaller galaxies\n• Evidence: stellar streams, chemical signatures\n\n**Galaxy Collisions:**\n• Common in the early universe, still happening today\n• Stars rarely collide (too far apart), but gas does\n• Collisions trigger intense star formation ('starburst')\n• Can transform spirals into ellipticals\n\n**The Milky Way-Andromeda Collision:**\n• Andromeda is approaching at 110 km/s\n• Collision in ~4.5 billion years\n• Galaxies will merge over 1-2 billion years\n• Result: 'Milkomeda,' a giant elliptical galaxy\n• Our solar system will likely survive (stars too spread out to collide)\n\n**Active Galactic Nuclei:**\n• When central black holes are actively feeding\n• Quasars: most luminous objects in the universe\n• Jets can extend millions of light-years\n• Feedback regulates galaxy growth"
