                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Dark Matter: The Hidden Scaffolding",
                                    content: "Galaxies reveal one of the universe's greatest mysteries: **dark matter**.\n\n**The Problem:**\n• Galaxy rotation curves: Stars orbit too fast at galaxy edges\n• Based on visible matter, outer stars should fly off\n• Something invisible provides extra gravitational pull\n\n**The Evidence:**\n• Rotation curves of spiral galaxies (flat, not declining)\n• Galaxy cluster dynamics (galaxies moving too fast)\n• Gravitational lensing (more mass than visible)\n• Cosmic Microwave Background patterns\n• Large-scale structure formation requires it\n\n**What We Know:**\n• ~27% of universe's mass-energy (vs. 5% ordinary matter)\n• Doesn't emit, absorb, or reflect light\n• Interacts gravitationally\n• Forms halos around galaxies\n• Not made of any known particle\n\n**Candidates:**\n• WIMPs (Weakly Interacting Massive Particles)\n• Axions\n• Primordial black holes\n• Modified gravity (alternative explanation)\n\nDark matter is the invisible scaffolding on which galaxies form and evolve."
