                                    type: "intro",
                                    title: "Becoming a Curious Character",
                                    content: "You've now journeyed through Richard Feynman's approach to thinking, learning, and living. But isolated techniques aren't enough—the magic happens when they work together.\n\nFeynman wasn't just curious. He wasn't just skeptical. He wasn't just hands-on. He was all of these things, integrated into a coherent way of engaging with the world.\n\nThis final lesson brings everything together: the childlike curiosity, the first principles thinking, the intellectual honesty, the learning by doing, the respectful questioning, and the joy of discovery.\n\nThe goal isn't to become Feynman—that's impossible and pointless. The goal is to develop YOUR version of these traits, adapted to your life, your interests, your personality.\n\nLet's integrate.",
