                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "How the Traits Reinforce Each Other",
                                    content: "These aren't separate skills—they're a system:\n\n**Curiosity â†’ Questions**\nChildlike curiosity generates the questions that drive everything else.\n\n**Questions â†’ First Principles**\nKeeping asking 'why?' leads naturally to fundamental truths.\n\n**First Principles â†’ Doing**\nOnce you understand fundamentals, you want to TEST them through action.\n\n**Doing â†’ Honesty**\nHands-on work reveals where your understanding is weak—you can't fake it.\n\n**Honesty â†’ Better Questions**\nAdmitting what you don't know opens new areas of curiosity.\n\n**Joy â†’ Sustainability**\nFinding pleasure in the process keeps you going when it gets hard.\n\n**The cycle:** Curiosity â†’ Questions â†’ Deep thinking â†’ Action â†’ Feedback â†’ Better questions â†’ More curiosity â†’ Joy â†’ More energy â†’ Deeper curiosity...\n\n**This is why Feynman never burned out:** The process itself was the reward.",
