                                    content: "You've learned how Feynman approached the world: with relentless curiosity, first principles thinking, intellectual honesty, hands-on engagement, productive skepticism, and above all—joy.\n\nBut knowledge without action is just entertainment.\n\nThe real question is: **What will YOU do with these ideas?**\n\nFeynman didn't read about being curious. He WAS curious. He didn't study intellectual honesty. He PRACTICED it. He didn't theorize about learning by doing. He DID things.\n\nThis final lesson is your bridge from learning to living. The adventures Feynman had aren't history—they're invitations. The universe is still full of mysteries. Problems still need first principles thinking. The joy of finding things out is available to anyone willing to seek it.\n\nYour adventures await.",
