                                    content: "Feynman left behind more than physics. He left a model of how to engage with the world:\n\n**What he proved possible:**\n• You can be brilliant AND playful\n• You can be rigorous AND joyful\n• You can question authority AND be productive\n• You can specialize AND be endlessly curious\n• You can understand deeply AND explain simply\n\n**What you can pass on:**\nEvery time you...\n• Ask a genuine question instead of pretending to know\n• Take something apart to understand it\n• Explain a concept simply to someone\n• Admit you were wrong\n• Find joy in confusion before clarity\n\n...you continue the Feynman legacy.\n\n**The ripple effect:** When you model curious, honest, joyful learning, others notice. Children, colleagues, friends—they see that it's possible to love learning without pretense.\n\n**The ultimate tribute:** Not memorizing Feynman quotes—but asking your own questions.",
