                                    content: "**Ancient Views:**\n• Egyptians discarded the brain during mummification—thought heart was the mind\n• Aristotle (350 BCE): Heart is seat of intelligence; brain is a cooling system\n• Galen (170 CE): First to argue brain controls behavior\n\n**Key Milestones:**\n• **1664:** Thomas Willis coins \"neurology\"; publishes brain anatomy atlas\n• **1791:** Galvani discovers \"animal electricity\"—nerves use electrical signals\n• **1848:** Phineas Gage's accident reveals frontal lobe controls personality\n• **1906:** Golgi and Cajal share Nobel Prize for neuron doctrine\n• **1949:** Hebb's Rule: \"Neurons that fire together, wire together\"\n• **1990s:** fMRI allows viewing brain activity in real-time\n• **2000s:** Optogenetics enables precise control of neurons with light\n• **2020s:** Brain-computer interfaces restore movement to paralyzed patients"
