                                    type: "intro",
                                    title: "The Feeling Brain",
                                    content: "Why does your heart race when you're scared? Why do you feel warmth when you see a loved one? Emotions aren't just abstract feelings—they're biological states generated by specific brain circuits. The limbic system, an ancient set of structures wrapped around the brainstem, creates your emotional life. Understanding this system reveals why we fall in love, why trauma lingers, and how emotions shape every decision we make."
