                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Lifestyle Factors for Brain Health",
                                    content: "**Physical Exercise**\n• Increases BDNF (brain-derived neurotrophic factor)\n• Promotes neurogenesis in hippocampus\n• Improves blood flow and oxygen delivery\n• Reduces inflammation\n• 30 min moderate exercise, 5x/week recommended\n\n**Sleep**\n• Clears toxic waste via glymphatic system\n• Consolidates memories\n• Synaptic pruning and strengthening\n• 7-9 hours for adults\n\n**Nutrition**\n• Omega-3 fatty acids (fish, flaxseed)\n• Antioxidants (berries, vegetables)\n• Mediterranean diet associated with lower dementia risk\n• Limit processed foods and sugar\n\n**Cognitive Engagement**\n• Lifelong learning builds cognitive reserve\n• Novel, challenging activities most beneficial\n• Social engagement protects against decline\n\n**Stress Management**\n• Chronic stress damages hippocampus\n• Elevated cortisol impairs memory\n• Meditation, relaxation, social support help"
