                                    type: "application",
                                    title: "Applying Neuroplasticity to Your Life",
                                    content: "**Learning More Effectively:**\n• Space practice over time (distributed practice)\n• Test yourself frequently (retrieval practice)\n• Sleep after learning (consolidation)\n• Make it challenging—struggle enhances plasticity\n• Combine with physical activity\n\n**Breaking Bad Habits:**\n• Understand it's a neural pathway, not a character flaw\n• Create new competing pathways through repetition\n• Change environmental cues that trigger old habits\n• Be patient—new pathways take time to strengthen\n\n**Recovery and Rehabilitation:**\n• Intensive, repetitive practice drives reorganization\n• Constraint-induced therapy: Force use of affected systems\n• Early intervention matters but late is still possible\n• Combine physical and cognitive rehabilitation\n\n**Mental Health:**\n• Therapy literally changes brain structure\n• Meditation increases prefrontal control over amygdala\n• Breaking rumination loops creates new thought patterns\n• Exercise is a powerful antidepressant"
