                                    content: "Your blood flows through two distinct circuits, each serving a critical purpose:\n\n**Pulmonary Circulation (Low Pressure)**\n• Right ventricle â†’ Pulmonary arteries â†’ Lungs â†’ Pulmonary veins â†’ Left atrium\n• Blood travels only 6 inches to the lungs\n• Pressure: ~25/8 mmHg (low to protect delicate lung capillaries)\n• Purpose: Gas exchange—COâ‚‚ out, Oâ‚‚ in\n\n**Systemic Circulation (High Pressure)**\n• Left ventricle â†’ Aorta â†’ Body tissues â†’ Vena cavae â†’ Right atrium\n• Blood must travel to distant extremities (head, toes)\n• Pressure: ~120/80 mmHg (high to reach all tissues)\n• Purpose: Deliver Oâ‚‚ and nutrients, remove waste\n\nThe **right heart** handles pulmonary circulation; the **left heart** powers systemic circulation."
