                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "The Electrocardiogram (ECG/EKG)",
                                    content: "The ECG records the heart's electrical activity through skin electrodes:\n\n**P Wave**\n• Represents **atrial depolarization**\n• SA node fires â†’ impulse spreads through atria\n• Duration: 0.08-0.10 seconds\n\n**PR Interval**\n• From start of P wave to start of QRS\n• Includes **AV nodal delay**\n• Normal: 0.12-0.20 seconds\n\n**QRS Complex**\n• Represents **ventricular depolarization**\n• Q = septal depolarization, R = main ventricular mass, S = late depolarization\n• Duration: 0.06-0.10 seconds (narrow = normal conduction)\n\n**T Wave**\n• Represents **ventricular repolarization**\n• Ventricles 'reset' for next beat\n\n**ST Segment**\n• Between QRS and T wave\n• Should be at baseline (elevation/depression = ischemia)"
