                                    content: "One complete heartbeat consists of coordinated phases:\n\n**Atrial Systole (0.1 sec)**\n• Atria contract, forcing blood into ventricles\n• Contributes ~20% of ventricular filling ('atrial kick')\n• AV valves open; semilunar valves closed\n\n**Ventricular Systole (0.3 sec)**\n• **Isovolumetric contraction** - All valves closed, pressure builds\n• **Ejection phase** - Semilunar valves open, blood ejected\n• AV valves closed (prevents backflow to atria)\n\n**Ventricular Diastole (0.4 sec)**\n• **Isovolumetric relaxation** - All valves closed, pressure falls\n• **Passive filling** - AV valves open, ventricles fill passively (80% of filling)\n• **Atrial kick** - Final 20% from atrial contraction\n\n**Key Terms:**\n• **Stroke Volume (SV)** - Volume ejected per beat (~70 mL)\n• **Ejection Fraction (EF)** - % of blood ejected (normal 55-70%)"
