                                    content: "**Blood pressure** is the force exerted by blood against vessel walls, measured in mmHg:\n\n**Systolic Pressure (Top Number)**\n• Peak pressure during ventricular contraction\n• Normal: <120 mmHg\n• Reflects cardiac output and arterial stiffness\n\n**Diastolic Pressure (Bottom Number)**\n• Minimum pressure during ventricular relaxation\n• Normal: <80 mmHg\n• Reflects peripheral resistance and arterial recoil\n\n**Pulse Pressure = Systolic - Diastolic**\n• Normal: 30-40 mmHg\n• Widened pulse pressure â†’ arterial stiffness (aging)\n\n**Mean Arterial Pressure (MAP)**\n• Average pressure throughout cardiac cycle\n• MAP = Diastolic + â…“(Pulse Pressure)\n• Or: MAP = â…“ Systolic + â…” Diastolic\n• Normal: 70-105 mmHg\n• Must be >60 mmHg to perfuse organs"
