                                    title: "Blood Components Overview",
                                    content: "Blood is a specialized connective tissue with two main components:\n\n**Plasma (55% of blood volume)**\n• Liquid matrix - 90% water\n• Contains dissolved proteins, nutrients, gases, electrolytes, hormones\n• Straw-colored when separated\n\n**Formed Elements (45% of blood volume)**\n• **Red Blood Cells (RBCs/Erythrocytes)** - 99% of formed elements\n• **White Blood Cells (WBCs/Leukocytes)** - <1% but crucial for immunity\n• **Platelets (Thrombocytes)** - Cell fragments for clotting\n\n**Hematocrit** = % of blood volume that is RBCs\n• Normal male: 42-52%\n• Normal female: 37-47%\n• Low = anemia; High = polycythemia\n\n**Blood Volume:** ~5 liters (7-8% of body weight)"
