                                    content: "The immediate response to exercise involves dramatic changes:\n\n**Heart Rate Response**\n• Resting: 60-100 bpm\n• Maximum: ~220 - age (estimate)\n• Can increase 3-4x within seconds\n• Controlled by sympathetic NS and circulating catecholamines\n\n**Stroke Volume Response**\n• Increases 30-50% during exercise\n• Due to: â†‘ venous return, â†‘ contractility\n• Plateaus at ~50-60% max effort\n\n**Cardiac Output (CO = HR × SV)**\n• Rest: ~5 L/min\n• Max exercise: 20-25 L/min (trained: up to 40 L/min!)\n• 5x increase in untrained; 8x in elite athletes\n\n**Blood Pressure Response**\n• Systolic: Increases to 200+ mmHg (higher workload)\n• Diastolic: Stays same or slightly decreases\n• Mean arterial pressure increases moderately"
