                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "The Skeletal System Divisions",
                                    content: "The skeleton is divided into two main parts:\n\n**Axial Skeleton (80 bones)**\nThe central axis of the body:\n• **Skull** (22 bones) - Protects brain, houses sensory organs\n• **Vertebral column** (26 bones) - Supports trunk, protects spinal cord\n• **Thoracic cage** (25 bones) - Ribs and sternum; protects heart/lungs\n• **Hyoid bone** (1) - Anchors tongue\n\n**Appendicular Skeleton (126 bones)**\nThe limbs and their attachments:\n• **Pectoral girdle** (4 bones) - Clavicles and scapulae\n• **Upper limbs** (60 bones) - Arms, forearms, hands\n• **Pelvic girdle** (2 bones) - Hip bones\n• **Lower limbs** (60 bones) - Thighs, legs, feet\n\n**Athletic Relevance:**\n• Axial skeleton = stability and core function\n• Appendicular skeleton = power generation and movement"
