                                    title: "Bone Health for Athletes",
                                    content: "Optimizing bone health is crucial for athletic performance:\n\n**Nutrition for Bone Health:**\n• **Calcium** - 1000-1300 mg/day (dairy, leafy greens, fortified foods)\n• **Vitamin D** - 600-1000 IU/day (sunlight, fatty fish, supplements)\n• **Protein** - Adequate intake supports bone matrix\n• **Vitamin K** - Helps calcium bind to bone\n\n**Training Considerations:**\n• **Impact loading** most effective for bone building\n• **Progressive overload** stimulates adaptation\n• **Multi-directional movements** strengthen bone in all planes\n• **Rest periods** allow remodeling to complete\n\n**Risk Factors for Poor Bone Health:**\n• Female athlete triad (energy deficiency, menstrual dysfunction, low BMD)\n• Relative Energy Deficiency in Sport (RED-S)\n• Low body weight\n• Amenorrhea\n• Smoking, excessive alcohol\n• Family history of osteoporosis"
