                                    explanation: "Abduction means moving a limb AWAY from the midline of the body. The term comes from Latin 'abducere' meaning 'to lead away.' The opposite movement—bringing the limb back toward the body—is adduction (think 'add' to the body). Flexion and extension occur in the sagittal plane (front-to-back movements)."
