                                    title: "The Cross-Bridge Cycle Detailed",
                                    content: "The molecular mechanism of contraction:\n\n**Step 1: Detachment**\n• ATP binds to myosin head\n• Causes conformational change\n• Myosin releases from actin\n• 'Rigor mortis' occurs without ATP!\n\n**Step 2: Cocking (Recovery Stroke)**\n• ATP hydrolyzed â†’ ADP + Pi\n• Energy stored in myosin head\n• Head pivots to 'cocked' position (90°)\n• Ready to bind actin\n\n**Step 3: Cross-Bridge Formation**\n• When Ca²âº present, binding sites exposed\n• Cocked myosin head attaches to actin\n• Forms cross-bridge\n• Pi released\n\n**Step 4: Power Stroke**\n• ADP released\n• Myosin head pivots (90° â†’ 45°)\n• Pulls actin filament toward M-line\n• Sarcomere shortens\n\n**Cycle repeats** ~5 times per second during contraction\nRequires ~1 ATP per cycle per myosin head"
