                                    content: "**Torque (Moment)** is rotational force:\n\n**Torque = Force × Lever Arm**\n• Lever arm = perpendicular distance from force to axis\n• Measured in Newton-meters (Nm)\n\n**Factors Affecting Torque:**\n• Magnitude of force\n• Distance from axis of rotation\n• Angle of force application (perpendicular = maximum)\n\n**Joint Torque:**\n• Muscle force × moment arm = joint torque\n• Moment arm changes throughout range of motion\n• Peak torque usually at mid-range\n• 'Sticking points' occur where moment arms are poor\n\n**External Torque:**\n• Load × distance from joint\n• Must be overcome by muscle torque\n• Same load feels 'heavier' at certain angles\n\n**Practical Applications:**\n• Closer grip = shorter moment arm = can lift more\n• Wider stance = different muscle moment arms\n• Why front raises are harder than lateral raises at different angles"
