                                    content: "Training affects all musculoskeletal tissues:\n\n**Bone Adaptations:**\n• **Increased bone mineral density (BMD)**\n• **Structural changes** - Thicker cortex, stronger trabecular architecture\n• **Site-specific** - Bones adapt where loaded\n• **Impact loading** most effective (running > cycling > swimming)\n\n**Tendon Adaptations:**\n• **Increased stiffness** - Better force transmission\n• **Cross-sectional area** - Thicker tendons\n• **Collagen turnover** - Stronger organization\n• **Slower than muscle** - 8-12+ weeks to see changes\n\n**Ligament Adaptations:**\n• **Limited but real** adaptation capacity\n• **Improved tensile strength**\n• **Takes longer than other tissues**\n• **Reason why proper progression matters**\n\n**Cartilage:**\n• **Most limited** adaptation capacity\n• **Moderate loading** may be beneficial\n• **Excessive loading** can be harmful\n• **Nutrition** (movement) essential for health"
