                                    explanation: "Neural adaptations occur first, often within days to weeks. These include improved motor unit recruitment, better synchronization, and decreased inhibition—essentially your nervous system learning to use your existing muscles more effectively. This is why beginners gain strength rapidly before visible muscle growth occurs. Hypertrophy takes 4-12 weeks, and connective tissue adaptations take even longer."
