                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Periodization: Organizing Training",
                                    content: "**Periodization** structures training for optimal adaptation:\n\n**Why Periodize?**\n• Prevent overtraining and burnout\n• Systematically develop different qualities\n• Peak performance for competition\n• Long-term athlete development\n\n**Basic Periodization Models:**\n\n**Linear Periodization:**\n• Gradual increase intensity, decrease volume\n• Classic model: Hypertrophy â†’ Strength â†’ Power\n• Best for beginners, single-peak sports\n\n**Undulating Periodization:**\n• Vary training stimuli within week/microcycle\n• Example: Heavy day, Light day, Moderate day\n• May produce better results in trained athletes\n\n**Block Periodization:**\n• Concentrated blocks focusing on specific qualities\n• Each block builds on the previous\n• Popular in elite sport\n\n**Key Periodization Concepts:**\n• **Macrocycle** - Full training year\n• **Mesocycle** - 3-6 week training block\n• **Microcycle** - Usually one week"
