                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "What Is Critical Thinking?",
                                    content: "Critical thinking is **the disciplined art of analyzing and evaluating information** to form well-reasoned judgments.\n\nIt's NOT:\n• Being negative or cynical\n• Criticizing everything\n• Ignoring emotions entirely\n• Having all the answers\n\nIt IS:\n• **Questioning assumptions** - Even your own\n• **Evaluating evidence** - Not just accepting claims\n• **Recognizing bias** - In yourself and others\n• **Reasoning logically** - Following valid arguments\n• **Remaining open-minded** - Willing to change your view\n\nThink of it as **mental quality control** - a filter between input and belief.",
