                                    content: "Your brain has two modes of operation:\n\n**System 1 (Fast Thinking)**\n• Automatic, effortless, intuitive\n• Excellent for: routine decisions, danger detection\n• Problem: Prone to errors, biases, manipulation\n\n**System 2 (Slow Thinking)**\n• Deliberate, effortful, analytical\n• Excellent for: complex problems, important decisions\n• Problem: Lazy, tires easily, often skipped\n\nCritical thinking requires **activating System 2** when System 1 wants to take shortcuts. Your brain will resist - it's trying to conserve energy. That's why critical thinking must be **practiced deliberately** until it becomes more automatic.",
