                                    content: "Before making important decisions, run through this checklist:\n\n**1. Confirmation Bias Check**\n\"Have I actively sought information that could prove me wrong?\"\n\n**2. Availability Check**\n\"Am I judging based on what's memorable, or actual data?\"\n\n**3. Anchoring Check**\n\"What would I think if I'd heard a completely different number first?\"\n\n**4. Dunning-Kruger Check**\n\"How much do I really know about this? What might I be missing?\"\n\n**5. Bias Blind Spot Check**\n\"Am I assuming I'm less biased than others? (You're not.)\"\n\n**The Ultimate Defense:**\nSeek out people who disagree with you and LISTEN. Not to argue - to understand. If you can't explain the opposing view accurately, you don't understand the issue well enough.",
