                                    content: "Use this template when presenting arguments:\n\n**1. CLAIM**: \"I believe/argue that [conclusion].\"\n\n**2. REASON**: \"Because [main supporting premise].\"\n\n**3. EVIDENCE**: \"This is supported by [specific evidence].\"\n\n**4. ACKNOWLEDGMENT**: \"I recognize that [counter-argument exists].\"\n\n**5. REBUTTAL**: \"However, [why conclusion still holds].\"\n\n**6. QUALIFICATION**: \"Therefore, it seems [likely/probable/certain] that [conclusion].\"\n\n**Example:**\n\"I believe remote work increases productivity (claim) because employees report fewer interruptions (reason). A Stanford study showed a 13% productivity boost (evidence). Critics argue collaboration suffers (acknowledgment), but data shows teams adapt their communication effectively (rebuttal). The evidence strongly suggests that remote work can boost productivity when properly implemented (qualified conclusion).\"",
