                                    content: "Our brains evolved for a world of **immediate physical threats** and small tribal groups. Quick decisions about danger were survival advantages. But these same shortcuts—fast, automatic, energy-efficient—cause systematic errors when applied to **complex modern decisions** like investing, hiring, or planning."
