                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "The Student Mindset",
                                    content: "Before success, the antidote to ego is the student mindset. A student knows they don't know. A student listens more than they talk. A student focuses on learning, not on looking smart. The greatest minds in history—from Epictetus to Benjamin Franklin—called themselves eternal students. This wasn't false modesty; it was strategic positioning for continuous growth."
