                                    type: "example",
                                    title: "Why Our Ancestors Breathed Better",
                                    content: "When scientists examine ancient skulls, they find something remarkable: **our ancestors had wide, open airways, straight teeth, and strong jaws.** They could breathe easily through their noses, even during sleep.\n\n**Modern skulls tell a different story:**\n• Narrower airways\n• Crooked teeth (90% of us)\n• Receding chins and weak jaws\n• Smaller nasal passages\n\n**What changed?** It wasn't genetics. It was:\n\n1. **Soft, processed food** - Less chewing = weaker jaw development\n2. **Indoor living** - Less nasal breathing stimulation\n3. **Mouth breathing habits** - Starting in childhood\n4. **Chronic congestion** - Allergies, pollution, infections\n\nThe good news: While we can't reshape our skulls overnight, we CAN retrain how we breathe - and the benefits start immediately.",
