                                    content: "Before we dive deeper into techniques, here are immediate changes you can make:\n\n**1. Close Your Mouth**\nThe single most important change. Your mouth is for eating and talking, not breathing. Practice keeping your lips gently closed throughout the day.\n\n**2. Check Your Night Breathing**\nDo you wake with a dry mouth? Snore? Wake tired? These are signs of mouth breathing during sleep. Consider mouth taping (we'll cover this later).\n\n**3. Slow Down**\nMost people take 12-20 breaths per minute. Optimal is closer to 5-6. Start noticing your breath rate without changing it.\n\n**4. Breathe Through Your Nose During Exercise**\nStart with low-intensity exercise (walking) while keeping your mouth closed. It will feel uncomfortable at first but gets easier.\n\n**The journey begins with awareness.** For the next 24 hours, simply notice: Am I breathing through my nose or mouth right now?"
