                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Nitric Oxide: The Secret Weapon",
                                    content: "Inside your nasal passages, special cells produce **nitric oxide (NO)** - a molecule so important that its discovery won the 1998 Nobel Prize in Medicine.\n\n**What nitric oxide does:**\n\n• **Kills bacteria and viruses** - It's a natural disinfectant\n• **Opens blood vessels** - Improves circulation\n• **Increases oxygen absorption** - Boosts O2 uptake by 10-25%\n• **Regulates blood pressure** - Keeps it in healthy range\n• **Supports immune function** - Fights infections\n\n**The problem:** When you breathe through your mouth, you get ZERO nitric oxide. None. The air bypasses your nose entirely.\n\n**The solution:** Every breath through your nose delivers a dose of this powerful molecule directly to your lungs. That's why nasal breathing during exercise actually improves performance, even though it feels harder at first.",
