                                    title: "The Bohr Effect: Why CO2 Matters",
                                    content: "Here's the counterintuitive science: **carbon dioxide (CO2) is not just a waste product - it's essential for oxygen delivery.**\n\n**The Bohr Effect:**\nHemoglobin (the molecule that carries oxygen in your blood) needs CO2 to RELEASE oxygen to your tissues. Without enough CO2, oxygen stays stuck on hemoglobin and never reaches your cells.\n\n**What happens when you over-breathe:**\n• You exhale too much CO2\n• Blood CO2 levels drop\n• Hemoglobin holds onto oxygen tighter\n• Less oxygen reaches your tissues\n• You feel like you need MORE air\n• You breathe faster (making it worse!)\n\n**The vicious cycle:** Over-breathing â†’ low CO2 â†’ poor O2 delivery â†’ breathlessness â†’ more over-breathing\n\n**The solution:** Slow breathing maintains optimal CO2 levels, allowing maximum oxygen delivery to every cell.",
