                                    type: "application",
                                    title: "How to Start Mouth Taping",
                                    content: "**What to use:**\n• Surgical tape (3M Micropore is popular)\n• Special mouth tape products (Somnifix, Hostage Tape)\n• NOT regular tape - it's too aggressive for skin\n\n**How to apply:**\n• Place a small strip vertically over the center of your lips\n• You don't need to cover the entire mouth\n• The tape is a gentle reminder, not a seal\n• You can easily open your mouth if needed\n\n**Safety considerations:**\n• Test during waking hours first\n• If you have severe sleep apnea, consult a doctor first\n• If you're congested, use nasal spray first or skip that night\n• Start with naps before doing all night\n\n**What to expect:**\n• First few nights may feel strange\n• You might remove it unconsciously at first\n• Within a week, it becomes comfortable\n• Soon you won't want to sleep without it",
