                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Pranayama: The Science of Life Force",
                                    content: "In Sanskrit, **Prana** means 'life force' and **Yama** means 'control.' Pranayama is the yogic art of controlling the breath to control life energy.\n\n**Key Pranayama Techniques:**\n\n**Nadi Shodhana (Alternate Nostril)**\n• Balances left/right brain\n• Calms nervous system\n• Clears nasal passages\n\n**Bhastrika (Bellows Breath)**\n• Rapid, forceful breaths\n• Energizing and warming\n• Increases CO2 tolerance\n\n**Kumbhaka (Breath Retention)**\n• Holding after inhale or exhale\n• Builds CO2 tolerance\n• Deepens meditative states\n\n**Ujjayi (Ocean Breath)**\n• Slight throat constriction\n• Creates resistance\n• Slows breathing naturally\n\nThe yogis understood intuitively what we now measure: different breathing patterns create different physiological and mental states.",
