                                    content: "In 2014, researchers injected Wim Hof and 12 people he trained with bacterial endotoxin (normally causes flu-like symptoms). The results made headlines:\n\n**Standard response** (control group):\n• Fever, headache, chills\n• Elevated inflammatory markers\n• Sick for hours\n\n**Wim Hof method practitioners:**\n• 50% lower inflammatory response\n• Minimal or no symptoms\n• Adrenaline levels 200% higher\n• Faster recovery\n\n**What this means:**\nWe can consciously influence our immune and inflammatory responses. This was previously thought impossible.\n\n**The technique used:** A simplified Tummo-style practice:\n1. 30-40 deep breaths\n2. Exhale and hold (1-3 minutes)\n3. Inhale deep, hold 15 seconds\n4. Repeat 3-4 rounds\n5. Combine with cold exposure",
