                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "The Five Core Principles",
                                    content: "No matter which techniques you choose, these principles are the foundation:\n\n**1. NOSE FIRST**\nBreathe through your nose whenever possible - walking, sleeping, even during moderate exercise.\n\n**2. SLOW DOWN**\nAim for 5-6 breaths per minute at rest. Slower is usually better.\n\n**3. BREATHE DEEP**\nUse your diaphragm. Let your belly expand on inhale. Your chest should barely move.\n\n**4. BUILD TOLERANCE**\nGradually train your CO2 tolerance through breath holds and reduced breathing.\n\n**5. PRACTICE DAILY**\nConsistency matters more than intensity. 5 minutes daily beats 30 minutes weekly.\n\nThese aren't rules to stress about - they're defaults to move toward. Be patient with yourself.",
