                                    content: "**Immediate Actions You Can Take:**\n\n**1. Check Your Crawlability (5 minutes)**\n• Visit yoursite.com/robots.txt - make sure important pages aren't blocked\n• Google 'site:yoursite.com' - see what's actually indexed\n• Look for 'indexed but not in sitemap' warnings in Search Console\n\n**2. Verify Your Pages Are Indexed (10 minutes)**\n• Go to Google Search Console â†’ Coverage\n• Check for 'Excluded' pages - these are crawled but not indexed\n• Look for errors preventing indexing\n\n**3. Analyze Search Intent for Your Keywords (15 minutes)**\n• Google your target keywords\n• Note what TYPE of content ranks (guides? products? lists?)\n• Ask: Does my content match this intent?\n\n**4. Submit Important Pages for Indexing**\n• In Search Console, use URL Inspection\n• Request indexing for new or updated pages\n• This speeds up the crawl queue\n\n**Remember:** SEO is a marathon, not a sprint. But understanding how the machine works is the first step to winning."
