                                    type: "example",
                                    title: "Keyword Research in Action",
                                    content: "**Case Study: Local Therapy Practice**\n\nA therapist in Austin wanted to rank for 'therapist' - a keyword with 200K monthly searches and impossible competition. Here's how we found better opportunities:\n\n**Step 1: Add Location**\n'therapist austin' â†’ 2,400/mo, KD 45 (still tough)\n\n**Step 2: Add Specialty**\n'anxiety therapist austin' â†’ 720/mo, KD 28 (achievable!)\n\n**Step 3: Find Long-tail Variations**\n• 'therapist for anxiety near me austin' â†’ 210/mo, KD 12\n• 'online anxiety therapist texas' â†’ 390/mo, KD 18\n• 'anxiety counselor austin tx' â†’ 170/mo, KD 15\n\n**Result:** Instead of one impossible keyword, they now had 15 rankable keywords totaling 3,000+ monthly searches - all highly targeted, local visitors who actually become clients.\n\n**The Pattern:** Start with what you offer, add location + specialty + modifiers to find achievable targets."
