                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Site Speed: Every Second Counts",
                                    content: "Page speed is a confirmed Google ranking factor, and it MASSIVELY impacts user experience.\n\n**The Speed Stats:**\n• 53% of mobile users abandon sites that take >3 seconds to load\n• 1-second delay = 7% reduction in conversions\n• Google aims to load pages in under 2.5 seconds\n\n**Core Web Vitals (Google's Speed Metrics):**\n\n**LCP - Largest Contentful Paint**\nHow long until the main content is visible\nGood: < 2.5 seconds\n\n**FID - First Input Delay**\nHow long until the page responds to interaction\nGood: < 100 milliseconds\n\n**CLS - Cumulative Layout Shift**\nHow much the page layout shifts while loading\nGood: < 0.1 (lower is better)\n\n**Quick Speed Wins:**\n• Compress images (use WebP format)\n• Enable browser caching\n• Minify CSS/JavaScript\n• Use a CDN (Content Delivery Network)\n• Upgrade to faster hosting\n\n**Test your speed:** PageSpeed Insights (pagespeed.web.dev)",
