                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Mobile-First Indexing",
                                    content: "Google now uses the MOBILE version of your site for indexing and ranking - even for desktop searches. If your mobile site is broken, your rankings will suffer.\n\n**What Mobile-First Means:**\n• Google's crawler acts like a mobile device\n• Your mobile content is what gets indexed\n• Mobile usability is a ranking factor\n\n**Mobile Optimization Checklist:**\n\n**Responsive Design**\n• Site adapts to any screen size\n• Same URL for mobile and desktop\n• Content is identical across devices\n\n**Touch-Friendly**\n• Buttons/links at least 48x48 pixels\n• Adequate spacing between tap targets\n• No hover-only functionality\n\n**Readable Without Zooming**\n• Font size minimum 16px\n• Content fits screen width\n• No horizontal scrolling\n\n**Test your mobile experience:** Google's Mobile-Friendly Test tool\n\n**Common Mobile Mistakes:**\n• Content hidden behind 'Read more' buttons (Google might not see it)\n• Pop-ups that cover content\n• Videos that don't play on mobile\n• Forms that are impossible to fill out",
