                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Schema Markup for Local Business",
                                    content: "**Schema markup** is code that helps search engines understand your content. For local businesses, **LocalBusiness schema** is essential.\n\n**Key schema properties:**\n```\n@type: \"MedicalBusiness\" or \"HealthAndBeautyBusiness\"\nname: Your Practice Name\naddress: Full address object\ntelephone: Phone number\nopeningHours: Business hours\ngeo: Latitude/longitude\npriceRange: $$ or $$$\nareaServed: Cities you serve\n```\n\n**Benefits of schema:**\n• Rich snippets in search results\n• Helps Google verify your NAP\n• Can display hours, reviews, services\n• Improves click-through rates\n\n**Implementation:** Add schema to your homepage and contact page. Use Google's Structured Data Testing Tool to verify. Most website platforms have plugins (Yoast, Rank Math) that add schema automatically."
