                                    type: "intro",
                                    title: "Your Digital Footprint",
                                    content: "Every time your business name, address, and phone number appear on another website, that's a **citation**. Citations are like votes of confidence that tell Google: 'Yes, this business exists at this location.'\n\n**Local links** take this further—when other local websites link to yours, it builds authority and relevance.\n\nTogether, citations and links account for about **23% of local ranking factors**. They're the backbone of proving to Google that your practice is legitimate, established, and trusted in your community.\n\nThe good news: building citations is systematic, predictable work. The challenge: consistency is everything.",
