                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Structured vs. Unstructured Citations",
                                    content: "**Structured citations** appear in business directories with consistent fields:\n• Name\n• Address\n• Phone\n• Website\n• Hours\n• Description\n\n**Examples:** Yelp, Yellow Pages, Psychology Today, Healthgrades\n\n**Unstructured citations** are mentions anywhere online:\n• Blog mentions\n• News articles\n• Event listings\n• Podcast show notes\n• Social media posts\n\n**Both matter for SEO:**\n• Structured = foundational consistency\n• Unstructured = natural, authoritative mentions\n\n**Quality > Quantity:** 50 accurate citations on authoritative sites beats 500 on spammy directories. Focus on sites Google trusts."
