                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Responding to Reviews: Best Practices",
                                    content: "**Respond to ALL reviews—positive and negative.**\n\nGoogle confirms that responding to reviews improves your ranking. It signals engagement and customer care.\n\n**Positive review responses:**\n• Thank them personally (use first name if given)\n• Keep it brief (2-3 sentences)\n• Never mention clinical details\n• Generic but warm\n\n**Example:** 'Thank you so much for your kind words. It's a privilege to support people on their journey, and I'm glad our work together has been helpful. Wishing you continued well-being.'\n\n**Negative review responses:**\n• Respond quickly (within 24-48 hours)\n• Stay calm and professional\n• Acknowledge their experience\n• Take it offline\n• Never get defensive or argue\n\n**Example:** 'I'm sorry to hear your experience didn't meet expectations. I take all feedback seriously. Please feel free to contact me directly at [email] so I can better understand and address your concerns.'\n\n**Never reveal** they're a client in your response."
