                                    title: "Fake and Unfair Reviews",
                                    content: "**Identifying fake/unfair reviews:**\n• Reviewer has no other reviews or history\n• Details don't match your practice\n• From a competitor or disgruntled non-client\n• Violates Google policies (hate speech, spam)\n\n**Flagging for removal:**\n1. Go to the review on Google Maps\n2. Click the three dots â†’ 'Flag as inappropriate'\n3. Select the policy violation reason\n4. Google reviews and may remove\n\n**Success rate:** Low for legitimate negative reviews, higher for obvious policy violations.\n\n**What NOT to do:**\n• Don't buy fake positive reviews\n• Don't have staff leave reviews\n• Don't ask friends/family who weren't clients\n• Don't retaliate publicly\n\n**Best defense against negative reviews:** Overwhelm them with positive ones. One bad review among 50 good ones barely registers. One bad review among 3 total is devastating."
