                                    title: "The Consulting Mindset Shift",
                                    content: "Million dollar consultants think differently:\n\n**Employee mindset:** 'What should I do today?'\n**Consultant mindset:** 'What outcome will I create?'\n\n**Vendor mindset:** 'Here's my rate, how many hours do you need?'\n**Partner mindset:** 'Let's discuss what success looks like for you'\n\n**Order-taker mindset:** 'What do you want me to do?'\n**Advisor mindset:** 'Here's what you should do, based on my expertise'\n\n**Key shifts:**\n• You are a peer to the buyer, not subordinate\n• You bring expertise they don't have\n• Your job is to improve their condition\n• You focus on outputs, not inputs\n• You're an investment, not an expense\n\n**Remember:** You're not selling your time. You're selling your ability to create specific, valuable outcomes that the client cannot achieve alone."
