                                    content: "Here's the paradox most consultants face: They spend 80% of their time pursuing leads and 20% doing actual consulting work. Million dollar consultants flip this: 20% marketing, 80% high-value work.\n\nThe difference? They've built systems that attract ideal clients rather than chasing anyone who might pay.\n\n**Ideal clients have these characteristics:**\n• They have budget and authority to hire you\n• They value expertise and pay premium fees\n• They're pleasant to work with\n• They lead to referrals and repeat business\n• They have problems you're uniquely suited to solve\n\nFinding these clients—and avoiding the rest—is the key to a thriving practice.",
