                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "The Referral System",
                                    content: "**Referrals are the lifeblood** of million dollar consulting. They arrive pre-sold, close faster, and pay higher fees.\n\n**Building a referral system:**\n\n**1. Ask explicitly**\n• 'Who else do you know who might benefit?'\n• Time it right: after delivering value\n• Make it easy: 'Would you be comfortable making an introduction?'\n\n**2. Create referral triggers**\n• Exceed expectations consistently\n• Stay top-of-mind (regular contact)\n• Be referable: clear value proposition\n\n**3. Expand referral sources**\n• Past clients (obvious)\n• Complementary consultants (non-competing)\n• Industry contacts\n• Professional service providers (accountants, lawyers)\n• Vendors who serve your target market\n\n**4. Reciprocate**\n• Refer business to referral sources\n• Create mutual benefit relationships\n\n**Goal:** Build a system where referrals arrive predictably, not randomly."
