                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Creating Your Three Options",
                                    content: "**Option 1: Basic**\n• Minimum viable engagement\n• Solves the core problem\n• No extras or follow-up\n• Lowest investment\n\n**Option 2: Recommended (Most choose this)**\n• Everything in Option 1\n• Added value enhancements\n• Better/faster results\n• Middle investment\n• **Label it 'Recommended'**\n\n**Option 3: Premium**\n• Everything in Options 1 + 2\n• Maximum value-add\n• Ongoing support/access\n• Highest investment\n\n**Pricing psychology:**\n• Option 1 anchors the floor\n• Option 3 anchors high value\n• Option 2 feels like the 'smart' choice\n• About 60% choose Option 2\n• About 25% choose Option 3\n• Only 15% choose Option 1\n\n**Result:** Higher average deal size than single-price proposals."
