                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Terms That Protect You",
                                    content: "**Payment terms (non-negotiable):**\n• 50% upon acceptance\n• 50% 45 days later (NOT upon completion)\n• Or: 100% upon acceptance with 5% discount\n\n**Why these terms:**\n• Confirms commitment\n• Covers your time investment\n• Avoids scope creep delays\n• Projects that don't start usually don't pay\n\n**Expense handling:**\n• Expenses billed as incurred (not marked up)\n• Or: expenses included in fee (simpler)\n\n**Important clauses:**\n• Cancellation policy (fee retained for time invested)\n• Intellectual property (you retain your methodologies)\n• Confidentiality (mutual)\n• Results not guaranteed (consulting, not insurance)\n\n**Never negotiate payment terms.** If they can't pay 50% upfront, they're probably not ready for consulting investment—or not the right client."
