                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Choosing Your Business Structure",
                                    content: "Your **business structure** affects taxes, liability, and paperwork. Here are the most common options for freelancers:\n\n**Sole Proprietorship:**\n• Default if you do nothing else\n• Simplest and cheapest to start\n• Personal liability for business debts\n• Business income on personal taxes\n• Best for: Low-risk, starting out\n\n**LLC (Limited Liability Company):**\n• Separates personal and business liability\n• More credibility with clients\n• Costs $50-500 to form (varies by state)\n• Can choose tax treatment\n• Best for: Most freelancers once established\n\n**S-Corporation:**\n• Can save self-employment taxes\n• Requires payroll, more complexity\n• Must pay yourself 'reasonable salary'\n• Best for: Earning $60K+ profit annually\n\n**Recommendation:** Start as sole proprietor, form an LLC once you're earning consistently, consider S-Corp election when profits justify the complexity."
