                                    content: "Freelancers need protection that employees take for granted:\n\n**Health Insurance:**\n• Healthcare.gov marketplace\n• Freelancers Union plans (in some states)\n• Spouse's employer plan\n• Professional association group plans\n\n**Professional Liability (Errors & Omissions):**\n• Covers claims of negligence or mistakes\n• Essential for consultants, designers, writers\n• Costs $500-2,000/year typically\n\n**General Liability:**\n• Covers accidents, injuries, property damage\n• Required if you meet clients in person\n• Often bundled with professional liability\n\n**Disability Insurance:**\n• Replaces income if you can't work\n• Often overlooked but critical\n• Freelancers have NO sick leave or workers' comp\n\n**The Freelancers Union** (founded by Horowitz) offers group rates for many of these. Don't skip insurance—one lawsuit or illness can destroy years of earnings."
