                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "The Six Client Sources",
                                    content: "Most freelance work comes from six primary channels. **Successful freelancers use multiple sources**—never rely on just one.\n\n**1. Your Network (Best Source)**\n• Past colleagues, friends, family connections\n• Highest trust, easiest close\n• Tell everyone you're freelancing\n\n**2. Referrals**\n• Existing clients recommend you\n• Pre-sold before they contact you\n• Ask for referrals proactively\n\n**3. Direct Outreach**\n• You contact potential clients\n• Cold email, LinkedIn, phone\n• Numbers game—volume matters\n\n**4. Content Marketing**\n• Blog, social media, speaking\n• Clients find YOU\n• Takes time but compounds\n\n**5. Freelance Platforms**\n• Upwork, Fiverr, Toptal\n• Easy to start, competitive\n• Good for building portfolio\n\n**6. Agencies/Subcontracting**\n• Work through other businesses\n• Steady flow, lower rates\n• Less client management"
