                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Pricing Models Compared",
                                    content: "Different pricing models work for different situations. Master all of them:\n\n**Hourly Rate:**\n• Pros: Simple, familiar, flexible for scope changes\n• Cons: Caps your earnings, penalizes efficiency\n• Best for: Ongoing work, unclear scope, maintenance\n\n**Project/Fixed Fee:**\n• Pros: Client knows total cost, rewards efficiency\n• Cons: Scope creep risk, requires accurate estimation\n• Best for: Defined deliverables, experienced freelancers\n\n**Retainer:**\n• Pros: Predictable income, ongoing relationship\n• Cons: Can limit availability for others\n• Best for: Regular ongoing work, strategic roles\n\n**Value-Based:**\n• Pros: Highest earning potential, aligned incentives\n• Cons: Requires confident positioning, harder to sell\n• Best for: High-impact work, measurable outcomes\n\n**The Evolution:** Most freelancers start hourly â†’ move to project-based â†’ graduate to value-based as they build expertise and confidence."
