                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Value-Based Pricing in Practice",
                                    content: "Value-based pricing requires understanding **what the work is worth to the client**:\n\n**Questions to Ask:**\n• 'What will this project help you achieve?'\n• 'If this succeeds, what's the financial impact?'\n• 'What's the cost of NOT doing this?'\n• 'What have you paid for similar projects before?'\n\n**The 10x Rule:**\nAim to deliver at least **10x the value** of what you charge. If your work will generate $100K, charging $10K is a bargain.\n\n**Example:**\nA consultant helps a company reduce employee turnover by implementing a retention program. \n• Cost of turnover: $50K per employee\n• Employees retained: 10\n• Value delivered: $500K\n• Consultant fee: $50K (10% of value)\n\nThe client gets a **10x ROI**. The consultant earns 5x what they'd make on hourly billing. Everyone wins.\n\n**Key:** You must be able to **articulate and quantify** the value. If you can't explain the ROI, you can't price on value."
