                                    content: "When prospects push back on price, **don't immediately discount**. Instead:\n\n**'That's more than I expected':**\n• 'I understand. Can you help me understand what you were expecting to invest?'\n• Then either justify the value or scope down\n\n**'Your competitor is cheaper':**\n• 'They may be. What specifically are you comparing?'\n• Differentiate on value, not price\n\n**'We don't have the budget':**\n• 'What budget do you have? Let's see what we can accomplish within it.'\n• Offer smaller scope, not lower rates\n\n**'Can you do it for [lower number]?':**\n• 'I can do [reduced scope] for that price. Which deliverables are most important?'\n• Never just say yes to lower price/same scope\n\n**The Golden Rule:**\nIf you lower price, **always reduce scope**. Otherwise you're just devaluing your work and training clients to negotiate."
