                                    title: "Deductions That Save You Money",
                                    content: "Freelancers can deduct business expenses, reducing taxable income. **Track everything**:\n\n**Home Office (if dedicated space):**\n• Percentage of rent/mortgage\n• Utilities, internet, phone\n• Must be EXCLUSIVE business use\n\n**Business Expenses:**\n• Software and subscriptions\n• Equipment (computer, camera, etc.)\n• Professional development, courses\n• Books related to your work\n• Professional memberships\n\n**Health Insurance (Huge!):**\n• Self-employed health insurance deduction\n• Can deduct 100% of premiums\n• Covers you, spouse, dependents\n\n**Travel:**\n• Business travel (airfare, hotel, meals)\n• Mileage for business driving (track it!)\n• Conference attendance\n\n**Retirement Contributions:**\n• SEP-IRA, Solo 401(k) contributions\n• Reduces taxable income AND builds wealth\n\n**Rule:** Keep receipts for everything. When in doubt, track it—your CPA can decide if it's deductible."
