                                    content: "Around **800,000 years ago**, humans domesticated fire—and everything changed. But not in the ways you might think:\n\n**The Cooking Revolution:**\n• Raw food takes 5 hours to chew daily; cooked food takes 1 hour\n• Cooking 'pre-digests' food externally, letting us shrink our guts\n• Smaller intestines = more energy for bigger brains\n• Cooking killed parasites and unlocked new food sources\n\n**The Power Shift:**\n• A human with fire could burn an entire forest\n• Fire kept predators away at night\n• It enabled migration to colder climates\n\n**The Dark Side:**\n• Even then, we were beginning to punch above our ecological weight\n• We gained power before gaining wisdom\n• The pattern of gaining technology before understanding consequences began here",
