                                    type: "example",
                                    title: "The Brain's Hidden Cost",
                                    content: "Our large brain seems like an obvious advantage. It wasn't. For millions of years, big brains were a **liability**:\n\n**The Energy Problem:**\n• Brain = 2% of body mass but uses **25% of energy** at rest\n• A chimp's brain uses only 8% of resting energy\n• Every calorie feeding your brain is stolen from muscles, immune system, or reproduction\n\n**The Birth Crisis:**\n• Big skulls can't fit through birth canals\n• Solution: Human babies are born 'premature' compared to other animals\n• A horse can walk hours after birth; humans need a year\n• This requires years of intensive parenting, limiting reproduction\n\n**The Muscle Trade-off:**\n• Energy for neurons = less energy for muscle\n• A chimp can rip a human apart despite being smaller\n• We traded raw strength for thinking power\n\n**The Verdict:** For millions of years, these costs outweighed the benefits. Big brains didn't guarantee survival.",
