                                    content: "**Patient Encounter:**\n\"Patient presents with RHINORRHEA, PHARYNGITIS, and bilateral OTITIS MEDIA.\"\n\n**Breaking it down:**\n• **RHINORRHEA** = RHIN/O (nose) + -RRHEA (discharge) = Runny nose\n• **PHARYNGITIS** = PHARYNG/O (throat) + -ITIS (inflammation) = Sore throat\n• **OTITIS MEDIA** = OT/O (ear) + -ITIS (inflammation) + MEDIA (middle) = Middle ear infection\n\n**Translation:** Patient has a runny nose, sore throat, and ear infections in both ears.\n\n**Coding implication:** Each condition gets its own ICD-10 code:\n• J00 - Acute nasopharyngitis (common cold with rhinorrhea)\n• J02.9 - Acute pharyngitis, unspecified\n• H66.93 - Otitis media, bilateral"
