                                    content: "The body is organized in a **hierarchy** from simple to complex:\n\n**1. CHEMICAL LEVEL** (atoms, molecules)\n• Atoms â†’ Molecules â†’ Macromolecules\n• Water, proteins, DNA, carbohydrates\n\n**2. CELLULAR LEVEL** (cells)\n• Basic unit of life\n• 200+ different cell types\n\n**3. TISSUE LEVEL** (tissues)\n• Groups of similar cells\n• 4 tissue types: Epithelial, Connective, Muscle, Nervous\n\n**4. ORGAN LEVEL** (organs)\n• Two or more tissue types working together\n• Heart, lungs, liver, stomach\n\n**5. ORGAN SYSTEM LEVEL** (organ systems)\n• Organs working together for a common function\n• 11 organ systems\n\n**6. ORGANISM LEVEL** (the whole body)\n• All systems working together = YOU"
