                                    title: "Atoms, Ions, and Bonds",
                                    content: "**ATOMIC STRUCTURE:**\n• **Protons** (+) and Neutrons (neutral) in nucleus\n• **Electrons** (-) orbit the nucleus\n• Atomic # = # of protons (defines element)\n\n**IONS:**\n• Atoms that gain or lose electrons\n• **Cations** = positive ions (lost electrons) Na+, K+, Ca2+\n• **Anions** = negative ions (gained electrons) Cl-, HCO3-\n\n**CHEMICAL BONDS:**\n\n**Ionic Bonds**\n• Electron transfer between atoms\n• Example: NaCl (table salt)\n• Break apart in water (electrolytes!)\n\n**Covalent Bonds**\n• Electron SHARING between atoms\n• Stronger than ionic bonds\n• Example: H2O, glucose, proteins\n\n**Hydrogen Bonds**\n• Weak attractions between polar molecules\n• Important in water properties and DNA structure"
