                                    content: "**pH SCALE:** 0-14 measures hydrogen ion (H+) concentration\n\n**ACIDS (pH < 7)**\n• Release H+ ions in water\n• Examples: Stomach acid (pH 1-2), vinegar\n• More H+ = lower pH = more acidic\n\n**BASES (pH > 7)**\n• Release OH- ions or absorb H+\n• Examples: Bleach, ammonia\n• Less H+ = higher pH = more basic/alkaline\n\n**NEUTRAL (pH = 7)**\n• Pure water\n• Equal H+ and OH-\n\n**BODY pH VALUES:**\n• Blood: 7.35-7.45 (slightly alkaline)\n• Stomach: 1.5-3.5 (highly acidic)\n• Urine: 4.5-8.0 (varies)\n\n**BUFFERS:**\n• Resist pH changes\n• Absorb excess H+ or OH-\n• Critical for blood pH homeostasis\n• Example: Bicarbonate buffer system"
