                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "The Plasma Membrane",
                                    content: "**STRUCTURE: Phospholipid Bilayer**\n• Two layers of phospholipids\n• Hydrophilic (water-loving) heads face out\n• Hydrophobic (water-fearing) tails face in\n• Embedded proteins for transport and signaling\n\n**FUNCTIONS:**\n• **Physical barrier** - separates cell from environment\n• **Selective permeability** - controls what enters/exits\n• **Communication** - receptor proteins receive signals\n• **Cell identification** - glycoproteins mark \"self\"\n\n**MEMBRANE PROTEINS:**\n• **Integral proteins** - embedded in membrane (channels, carriers)\n• **Peripheral proteins** - attached to surface (enzymes, structural)\n• **Glycoproteins** - with carbohydrate chains (recognition)\n\n**FLUID MOSAIC MODEL:**\nMembrane is fluid (phospholipids move) with mosaic of proteins"
