                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Epithelial Tissue",
                                    content: "**FUNCTIONS:** Cover surfaces, line cavities, form glands\n\n**CHARACTERISTICS:**\n• Cells tightly packed with minimal matrix\n• Avascular (no blood vessels) - relies on diffusion\n• High regeneration ability\n• Attached to basement membrane\n\n**CLASSIFICATION BY SHAPE:**\n• **Squamous** - flat, scale-like\n• **Cuboidal** - cube-shaped\n• **Columnar** - tall, column-like\n\n**CLASSIFICATION BY LAYERS:**\n• **Simple** - one layer (diffusion, filtration)\n• **Stratified** - multiple layers (protection)\n• **Pseudostratified** - appears layered but isn't\n\n**EXAMPLES:**\n• Simple squamous â†’ alveoli, blood vessels\n• Stratified squamous â†’ skin, mouth, esophagus\n• Simple columnar â†’ stomach, intestines\n• Pseudostratified columnar â†’ respiratory tract"
