                                    content: "**FUNCTION:** Movement through contraction\n\n**THREE TYPES:**\n\n**1. SKELETAL MUSCLE**\n• Attached to bones\n• Voluntary control\n• Striated (striped) appearance\n• Long, cylindrical, multinucleated cells\n• Example: Biceps, quadriceps\n\n**2. CARDIAC MUSCLE**\n• Heart only\n• Involuntary\n• Striated\n• Branched cells with intercalated discs\n• Example: Myocardium\n\n**3. SMOOTH MUSCLE**\n• Walls of hollow organs\n• Involuntary\n• Non-striated (no stripes)\n• Spindle-shaped cells\n• Example: Blood vessels, GI tract, bladder\n\n**Memory Tip:**\nSkeletal = Striated + Voluntary\nCardiac = Striated + Involuntary + Branched\nSmooth = Non-striated + Involuntary + Visceral"
