                                    content: "**SPINAL CORD:**\n• Extends from brainstem to L1-L2\n• Protected by vertebral column\n• Gray matter inside (H-shaped) - cell bodies\n• White matter outside - myelinated axons\n\n**31 PAIRS OF SPINAL NERVES:**\n• 8 Cervical (C1-C8)\n• 12 Thoracic (T1-T12)\n• 5 Lumbar (L1-L5)\n• 5 Sacral (S1-S5)\n• 1 Coccygeal\n\n**CRANIAL NERVES:**\n• 12 pairs, originate from brain\n• CN I - Olfactory (smell)\n• CN II - Optic (vision)\n• CN VII - Facial (expressions)\n• CN X - Vagus (parasympathetic)\n\n**Mnemonic for Cranial Nerves:**\n\"On Old Olympus' Towering Top A Finn And German Viewed Some Hops\"\n(Olfactory, Optic, Oculomotor, Trochlear, Trigeminal, Abducens, Facial, Acoustic, Glossopharyngeal, Vagus, Spinal Accessory, Hypoglossal)"
