                                    content: "**LYMPH:**\n• Clear fluid (filtered from blood plasma)\n• Contains WBCs, especially lymphocytes\n• No RBCs (unless injury)\n\n**LYMPHATIC VESSELS:**\n• Lymphatic capillaries (very permeable)\n• Collecting vessels (have valves)\n• Trunks and ducts\n• Right lymphatic duct â†’ right upper body\n• Thoracic duct â†’ rest of body (larger)\n\n**LYMPH NODES:**\n• Bean-shaped filter stations\n• Contain macrophages and lymphocytes\n• Filter pathogens and debris\n• Swell when fighting infection (\"swollen glands\")\n\n**LYMPHOID ORGANS:**\n• **Thymus** - T cell maturation (shrinks with age)\n• **Spleen** - filters blood, stores platelets\n• **Tonsils** - first line defense in throat\n• **MALT** - Mucosa-Associated Lymphoid Tissue (Peyer's patches in intestine)"
