                                    content: "**PRIMARY ORGANS - TESTES:**\n• Produce sperm (spermatogenesis)\n• Produce testosterone\n• Located in scrotum (cooler temperature needed)\n• Seminiferous tubules - Sperm production\n• Interstitial (Leydig) cells - Testosterone production\n\n**ACCESSORY STRUCTURES:**\n• **Epididymis** - Sperm maturation & storage\n• **Vas (Ductus) Deferens** - Transports sperm\n• **Ejaculatory Duct** - Joins vas deferens + seminal vesicle\n• **Urethra** - Shared pathway (urine & semen)\n\n**ACCESSORY GLANDS:**\n• **Seminal Vesicles** - Fructose-rich fluid (~60% of semen)\n• **Prostate Gland** - Slightly alkaline fluid (~30%)\n• **Bulbourethral (Cowper's)** - Pre-ejaculate lubricant\n\n**HORMONAL CONTROL:**\n• GnRH (hypothalamus) â†’ FSH + LH (anterior pituitary)\n• FSH â†’ Stimulates spermatogenesis\n• LH â†’ Stimulates testosterone production"
