                                    content: "**~28-DAY CYCLE (varies):**\n\n**UTERINE PHASES:**\n\n**1. Menstrual Phase (Days 1-5)**\n• Endometrium sheds (menstruation)\n• Low estrogen and progesterone\n\n**2. Proliferative Phase (Days 6-14)**\n• Endometrium rebuilds\n• Rising estrogen (from growing follicle)\n• Ends with OVULATION (Day ~14)\n\n**3. Secretory Phase (Days 15-28)**\n• Endometrium prepares for implantation\n• Corpus luteum produces progesterone\n• If no pregnancy â†’ Corpus luteum degenerates â†’ Hormones drop â†’ Menstruation\n\n**OVARIAN PHASES:**\n• Follicular phase (Days 1-14) - Follicle develops\n• Ovulation (Day ~14) - LH surge triggers egg release\n• Luteal phase (Days 15-28) - Corpus luteum forms\n\n**KEY HORMONES:**\n• FSH - Follicle development\n• LH - Triggers ovulation\n• Estrogen - Endometrial growth\n• Progesterone - Maintains endometrium"
