                                    content: "**THE HEALTH RECORD AS LEGAL DOCUMENT:**\n\n**Ownership:**\n• Healthcare facility OWNS the physical record\n• Patient OWNS the information (has access rights)\n\n**Legal Functions:**\n• Business record of the organization\n• Evidence of care provided\n• Basis for reimbursement\n• Defense in malpractice suits\n\n**Documentation Requirements:**\n• **Timely** - Document as close to event as possible\n• **Accurate** - Reflect what actually occurred\n• **Complete** - All relevant information included\n• **Legible** - Readable by all users\n• **Authenticated** - Signed/dated by author\n\n**Legal Principles:**\n• \"If it wasn't documented, it wasn't done\"\n• Records can be subpoenaed\n• Alterations must follow proper procedures\n• Never backdate entries\n• Late entries should be labeled as such"
