                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Sequencing Rules for Neoplasms",
                                    content: "**WHEN NEOPLASM IS REASON FOR ENCOUNTER:**\n\n**1. Treatment of Primary Site:**\n• Code primary malignancy first\n• Even if metastasis present\n\n**2. Treatment of Secondary Site:**\n• Code secondary site being treated first\n• Then code primary site\n\n**3. Primary Unknown (C80.1):**\n• Use when metastasis present\n• But primary cannot be determined\n• Sequence: Secondary site, then C80.1\n\n**4. Admission for Complications:**\n• Code complication first (e.g., anemia)\n• Then neoplasm code\n\n**CHEMOTHERAPY/RADIATION ENCOUNTERS:**\n• Z51.11 (chemo) or Z51.0 (radiation) first\n• Then neoplasm code\n\n**HISTORY OF MALIGNANCY:**\n• Z85.x when treatment completed\n• No evidence of disease\n• Cancer \"in remission\" uses active code"
