                                    title: "Surgical Pathology Levels",
                                    content: "**SURGICAL PATHOLOGY LEVELS** (Based on tissue complexity):\n\n**Level I (88300)** - Gross examination only:\n• Specimens not requiring microscopic exam\n\n**Level II (88302)** - Gross and microscopic:\n• Appendix (incidental), skin tags, foreskin\n\n**Level III (88304)**:\n• Gallbladder, tonsils, adenoids\n• Simple tissue with limited pathology\n\n**Level IV (88305)** - Most common:\n• Breast biopsy, colon biopsy, skin with tumor\n• Detailed microscopic examination needed\n\n**Level V (88307)**:\n• Breast mastectomy, colon resection\n• Complex specimens requiring extensive work\n\n**Level VI (88309)**:\n• Most complex specimens\n• Fetal tissue, exenteration specimens\n\n**Billing Note**: Only ONE level per specimen - no unbundling!"
