                                    title: "Case Study 1: Office Visit with Procedure",
                                    content: "**Clinical Scenario**:\nEstablished patient presents with painful plantar wart. Physician examines, discusses treatment options, and performs cryosurgery destruction. Total time: 25 minutes.\n\n**Documentation Review**:\n• Chief complaint: Plantar wart, left foot\n• Exam: 1.5 cm verruca on plantar surface\n• Treatment: Liquid nitrogen cryotherapy\n• Assessment: Viral wart (B07.0)\n\n**Code Assignment**:\n\n**E/M Service**:\n• 25 min with procedure â†’ evaluate MDM or time\n• Straightforward problem, minimal risk\n• However, procedure is minor (0-day global)\n• E/M separately billable with -25\n\n**Final Codes**:\n• **99213-25** (E/M, established, low complexity, with -25)\n• **17110** (Destruction benign lesions, 1-14)\n• **ICD-10: B07.0** (Plantar wart)"
