                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Common Ambulatory Coding Pitfalls",
                                    content: "**COMMON ERRORS TO AVOID**:\n\n**1. Unbundling**:\n• Separately billing components that are bundled\n• Use NCCI edits to check bundling rules\n\n**2. Missing Modifiers**:\n• Forgetting -25 on E/M with same-day procedure\n• Not using -59 when services are truly distinct\n• Missing laterality (-RT, -LT, -50)\n\n**3. Incorrect E/M Level**:\n• Upcoding without documentation support\n• Downcoding and losing appropriate revenue\n• Using time when MDM supports higher level\n\n**4. Diagnosis Mismatch**:\n• Linking wrong ICD-10 to procedure\n• Missing medical necessity support\n\n**5. Global Period Violations**:\n• Billing E/M during global without modifier\n• Not using -24, -78, -79 appropriately\n\n**COMPLIANCE TIP**: When in doubt, query the provider!"
