                                {
                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Status Indicators",
                                    content: "**Determines how services are paid:**\n\n**S - Significant Procedure:**\nPaid under OPPS, not discounted\n\n**T - Surgical Procedure:**\nMultiple procedure reduction applies (50%)\n\n**V - Visit (Clinic/ED):**\nSeparately payable medical visit\n\n**J1 - Hospital Part B:**\nComprehensive APC, packages other services\n\n**Q1-Q4 - Composite APCs:**\nSeparate composite payment policies\n\n**N - Packaged:**\nNot separately payable, bundled into another APC\n\n**B - Bundled Always:**\nPayment included in other services"
                                },
                                {
                                    type: "example",
                                    title: "Outpatient Visit Billing",
                                    content: "**ED Visit with Multiple Services:**\n\nPatient: Chest pain evaluation\n\n**Services Provided:**\n• Level 4 ED visit (99284) - Status V\n  APC 5024, Payment: $512\n\n• Chest X-ray (71046) - Status Q1\n  APC 5521, Payment: $23\n\n• ECG (93000) - Status S\n  APC 5721, Payment: $14\n\n• Troponin lab (84484) - Status Q4\n  Packaged into visit, $0 separate\n\n**Total Facility Payment:** $549\n\n*Plus separate physician professional fees*"
                                },
                                {
                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "OPPS Special Topics",
                                    content: "**Observation Services:**\n• Must meet Medicare criteria\n• Billed with G-codes\n• May convert to inpatient if criteria met\n\n**Pass-Through Payments:**\n• New drugs, biologics, devices\n• Temporary separate payment\n• Eventually folded into APC rates\n\n**Outlier Payments:**\n• Cost exceeds threshold\n• Additional payment beyond APC\n\n**Bilateral Procedures:**\n• Modifier 50\n• Payment adjustments apply\n\n**Conditional Packaging:**\n• Some services packaged only when billed with certain others"
                                },
                                {
                                    type: "quiz",
                                    title: "Knowledge Check",
                                    question: "What is a key difference between APCs and MS-DRGs?",
                                    options: [
                                        { text: "APCs pay more than DRGs", correct: false },
                                        { text: "Multiple APCs can be billed for one visit; one DRG covers entire stay", correct: true },
                                        { text: "APCs are only for surgical patients", correct: false },
                                        { text: "DRGs apply to outpatient services only", correct: false }
                                    ],
                                    explanation: "A single **DRG** provides one bundled payment for an entire inpatient stay, regardless of services. Under **OPPS/APCs**, each separately payable service generates its own APC, so multiple APCs can be billed for one outpatient encounter. This fundamental structure difference affects how coding impacts payment."
                                }
