                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Lean vs Six Sigma",
                                    content: "Lean: Focuses on eliminating waste and improving flow. Faster cycle times, reduced steps. Six Sigma: Focuses on reducing variation and defects. Data-driven, statistical tools. Lean Six Sigma: Combines both approaches for comprehensive improvement."
